      "confidence": 0.55,
      "curator_note": "rule_index cross-links equation 4.5 to IMS_4_5: [C]1(H2,H3,H4)[C]5(H6,H7){-}[C+.]8(H10,H11)[C]12(H13,H14,H15) >> [C]1(H2,H3,H4)[C.]5(H6,H7).[C+]8(H10,H11)[C]12(H13).[H]14[H]15. Bond changes MATCH the book: cleave the C5-C8 (central C-C) bond, lose H14+H15 as H2 from the terminal methyl C12 (1,1), leaving the C2H3 cation. CAVEATS: the rule localises +. on a 4-coordinate carbon C8 (hypervalent, RDKit-invalid, hence the neutral-skeleton precursor here) and its C2H3+ product omits the C8=C12 double bond (no {=}), leaving C12 under-coordinated -- a mild encoding defect. Net transformation is faithful."
